<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "Walking into an empty space posts a card in the conversation it belongs to. It is how everybody reading finds out that something is happening in there, and it is a message like any other: it stays in the scrollback, and somebody scrolling past tomorrow still sees it."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_community}>{dgettext("help_space", "While it lasts")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "The card counts who is inside and names a few of them, and it keeps up on its own as people come and go. Walking into a space somebody is already in posts nothing: one gathering, one card."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_clock}>{dgettext("help_space", "Once everybody has gone")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "The same card becomes the record of what happened: how long the gathering ran, and how many different people came. The address itself does not expire — a space is a place — so the entry beside the tabs still posts a card for it, and the next person in starts a new gathering."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_link}>{dgettext("help_space", "Who posts one")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "Only a registered nickname. A shared address carries somebody accountable for it, which is the same rule every other link in this chat follows. A guest walks into the space exactly as usual; there is simply no card, because there is nobody to put on it."
  )}
</p>

<p>
  {dgettext("help_space", "See also:")}
  <.help_link topic="feature-virtual-spaces">
    {dgettext("help_space", "Virtual Spaces")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-space-tab">
    {dgettext("help_space", "A Space in Its Own Tab")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-space-share">
    {dgettext("help_space", "Inviting Someone to a Space")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
